        i.fa(class="{{#if allowsPersonalListWidth}}fa-check{{else}}fa-square-o{{/if}}")
        span
          i.fa.fa-arrows-h
          | {{_ 'personal-list-width'}}

//- Board Settings / Card - what the opened card and the minicard show, and
  in what order. Opened from the board's cog menu (boardMenuPopup above); it
  used to be split across the CARD's own menu ("Show on Card", side="card")
  and the MINICARD's own menu ("Show on Minicard", side="minicard"), and
  settingsSideClass() still hides one column when a side is passed.
  "Labels text" - the one PERSONAL setting here - stays reachable by a
  non-admin, who is passed `personalOnly=true` so every board-wide,
  admin-only row is hidden and only that one shows. client/lib/minicardLabelText.js
//- ONE heading, "Card field order", over TWO lists: "Show on Minicard" in
  the board's minicard order and "Show on Card" in its card order. The lists
  are independent because the orders are: a field can sit third on the
  minicard and last on the card. Every row of either list is
  `[checkbox] [up] [down] icon label` - the checkbox is whether that side
  shows the field, the arrows move it on THAT side only, and the icon and
  label are the field's own (models/lib/cardSettingsRows.js). The rows are
  not written out here: the two `each` loops draw them from that table in
  the order models/lib/cardFieldOrder.js resolves for the board, the SAME
  source cardDetails.jade and minicard.jade render from, so what the popup
  lists top to bottom is what the card and the minicard draw top to bottom.
  A row whose arrows would do nothing (the card's title bar and its
  galleries, a minicard row that modifies another element rather than being
  one) keeps them, disabled, so every row reads the same.
  Up/down buttons rather than a drag library: no sortable-based reorder of a
  plain settings LIST exists elsewhere in this codebase to reuse, so buttons
  are the simpler, safer mechanism. Keyboard-reachable: `href="#"` and
  `role="button"`, titled with the existing move-up/move-down keys.
  client/components/sidebar/sidebar.js, tests/cardSettingsCoverage.test.cjs
template(name="boardCardSettingsPopup")
  form.board-card-settings(class=settingsSideClass)
    h4.card-field-order-heading {{_ 'card-field-order'}}
    .card-field-order-columns
      .card-field-order-column.card-field-order-column-minicard
        h4.card-field-order-column-heading {{_ 'show-on-minicard'}}
        each row in minicardSettingsRows
          .card-field-order-row.js-card-field-order-row(class="{{#if row.personal}}card-settings-row-personal{{/if}}" data-key="{{row.key}}" data-side="minicard")
            a.flex.card-field-order-toggle(class=row.toggle class="{{#if row.checked}}is-checked{{/if}}" title="{{row.title}}")
              i.fa(class="{{#if row.checked}}fa-check{{else}}fa-square-o{{/if}}")
            if canModifyBoard
              a.flex.card-field-order-move.js-card-field-order-up(href="#" role="button" class="{{#unless row.canMoveUp}}is-disabled{{/unless}}" title="{{_ 'card-field-order-move-up'}}" aria-label="{{_ 'card-field-order-move-up'}}")
                i.fa.fa-arrow-up
              a.flex.card-field-order-move.js-card-field-order-down(href="#" role="button" class="{{#unless row.canMoveDown}}is-disabled{{/unless}}" title="{{_ 'card-field-order-move-down'}}" aria-label="{{_ 'card-field-order-move-down'}}")
                i.fa.fa-arrow-down
            span.card-field-order-label
              each icon in row.icons
                i.fa(class=icon)
              | {{row.title}}
              //- The user's own override of the board's "Labels text" default,
                tri-state: it says whether it is following the board or
                overriding it, with a way back to "follow the board" rather
                than cycling the checkbox through both states again.
              if row.labelTextOverride
                if hasLabelTextOverride
                  | &nbsp;
                  a.js-reset-minicard-label-text-override(title="{{_ 'label-text-use-board-default'}}")
                    | ({{_ 'label-text-overridden'}})
                else
                  | &nbsp;({{_ 'label-text-follows-board'}})
      .card-field-order-column.card-field-order-column-card
        h4.card-field-order-column-heading {{_ 'show-on-card'}}
        each row in cardSettingsRows
          .card-field-order-row.js-card-field-order-row(data-key="{{row.key}}" data-side="card")
            a.flex.card-field-order-toggle(class=row.toggle class="{{#if row.checked}}is-checked{{/if}}" title="{{row.title}}")
              i.fa(class="{{#if row.checked}}fa-check{{else}}fa-square-o{{/if}}")
            if canModifyBoard
              a.flex.card-field-order-move.js-card-field-order-up(href="#" role="button" class="{{#unless row.canMoveUp}}is-disabled{{/unless}}" title="{{_ 'card-field-order-move-up'}}" aria-label="{{_ 'card-field-order-move-up'}}")
                i.fa.fa-arrow-up
              a.flex.card-field-order-move.js-card-field-order-down(href="#" role="button" class="{{#unless row.canMoveDown}}is-disabled{{/unless}}" title="{{_ 'card-field-order-move-down'}}" aria-label="{{_ 'card-field-order-move-down'}}")
                i.fa.fa-arrow-down
            span.card-field-order-label
              each icon in row.icons
                i.fa(class=icon)
              | {{row.title}}

//- The board's Subtasks Settings. Its own template, because the same settings
  are read from two places: Board Settings, and the menu of a subtask on an
  opened card - which is where somebody looking at a subtask is when they want
  to change what subtasks do. One list, one set of handlers.
  client/components/cards/subtasks.jade
template(name="boardSubtaskSettingsBody")
  form.board-subtask-settings
    h3 {{_ 'show-parent-in-minicard'}}
      a#prefix-with-full-path.flex.js-field-show-parent-in-minicard(title="{{_ 'prefix-with-full-path'}}" class="{{#if $eq presentParentTask 'prefix-with-full-path'}}is-checked{{/if}}")
        i.fa(class="{{#if $eq presentParentTask 'prefix-with-full-path'}}fa-check{{else}}fa-square-o{{/if}}")
        span {{_ 'prefix-with-full-path'}}
      a#prefix-with-parent.flex.js-field-show-parent-in-minicard(title="{{_ 'prefix-with-parent'}}" class="{{#if $eq presentParentTask 'prefix-with-parent'}}is-checked{{/if}}")
        i.fa(class="{{#if $eq presentParentTask 'prefix-with-parent'}}fa-check{{else}}fa-square-o{{/if}}")
        span {{_ 'prefix-with-parent'}}
      a#subtext-with-full-path.flex.js-field-show-parent-in-minicard(title="{{_ 'subtext-with-full-path'}}" class="{{#if $eq presentParentTask 'subtext-with-full-path'}}is-checked{{/if}}")
        i.fa(class="{{#if $eq presentParentTask 'subtext-with-full-path'}}fa-check{{else}}fa-square-o{{/if}}")
        span {{_ 'subtext-with-full-path'}}
      a#subtext-with-parent.flex.js-field-show-parent-in-minicard(title="{{_ 'subtext-with-parent'}}" class="{{#if $eq presentParentTask 'subtext-with-parent'}}is-checked{{/if}}")
        i.fa(class="{{#if $eq presentParentTask 'subtext-with-parent'}}fa-check{{else}}fa-square-o{{/if}}")
        span {{_ 'subtext-with-parent'}}
      a#no-parent.flex.js-field-show-parent-in-minicard(title="{{_ 'no-parent'}}" class="{{#if $eq presentParentTask 'no-parent'}}is-checked{{/if}}")
        i.fa(class="{{#if $eq presentParentTask 'no-parent'}}fa-check{{else}}fa-square-o{{/if}}")
        span {{_ 'no-parent'}}
    div
      hr

    div.check-div
      a.flex.js-field-has-subtasks(title="{{_ 'show-subtasks-field'}}" class="{{#if allowsSubtasks}}is-checked{{/if}}")
        i.fa(class="{{#if allowsSubtasks}}fa-check{{else}}fa-square-o{{/if}}")
        span {{_ 'show-subtasks-field'}}

    label
      | {{_ 'deposit-subtasks-board'}}
      select.js-field-deposit-board(disabled="{{#unless allowsSubtasks}}disabled{{/unless}}")
          each boards
            if isBoardSelected
              option(value=_id selected="selected") {{title}}
            else
              option(value=_id) {{title}}
          if isNullBoardSelected
            option(value='null' selected="selected") {{_ 'custom-field-dropdown-none'}}
          else
            option(value='null') {{_ 'custom-field-dropdown-none'}}
    div
      hr

    label
      | {{_ 'deposit-subtasks-list'}}
      select.js-field-deposit-list(disabled="{{#unless hasLists}}disabled{{/unless}}")
          each lists
            if isListSelected
              option(value=_id selected="selected") {{title}}
            else
              option(value=_id) {{title}}

template(name="boardSubtaskSettingsPopup")
  +boardSubtaskSettingsBody

//- #1173: the fourteen per-source links that were here are the import PAGE now
  - one full-width page that lists every source, offers the same "what to
  include" checkboxes every export offers, and keeps its own address per source
  so the old links still work. What is left in the popup is the one import that
  is not a board: card dependencies.
template(name="chooseBoardSourcePopup")
  ul.pop-over-list
    li
      //- "Import board", and nothing else. It used to read "Import board
        (Trello, Jira, WeKan export, CSV, Excel, ...)" - the whole list of
        sources, in a menu row, above a page that asks which source it is and
        lists every one of them with room to. Naming them twice makes the menu
        the thing to read and the page the thing to confirm.
        client/components/import/import.jade
      a.js-open-import-page(href="{{pathFor '/import'}}")
        i.fa.fa-download
        |  {{_ 'import-board-c'}}
    li
      a.js-import-dependencies {{_ 'import'}} / {{_ 'card-dependencies'}} (JSON/SVG)

template(name="importDependenciesPopup")
  form.js-import-dependencies-form
    label
      | {{_ 'r-board'}}
      select.js-import-dependencies-board
        each boardsForDependencyImport
          option(value="{{_id}}") {{title}}
    label
      | {{_ 'import-dependencies-file'}}
      input.js-import-dependencies-file(type="file" accept=".json,.svg,application/json,image/svg+xml")
    textarea.js-import-dependencies-text(rows="6" placeholder="{{_ 'import-dependencies-placeholder'}}")
    button.primary.confirm.js-import-dependencies-submit(type="submit") {{_ 'import'}}
    if importResult
      p.quiet.js-import-dependencies-result {{importResult}}

